6. **Dependency review.** The new packages and their transitive additions: from `web/package-lock.json` (the +359/-4) and `HpsmPoc.Api.csproj` + the restore's `project.assets.json`: name, exact version, licence (read each `package.json` `license` / the `.nuspec`), publish date (read-only registry GET only; the builder says exporter beta.46 = 16 days old and `@opentelemetry/api` pinned to 1.9.1 as 1.10.0 is 2 days old), install scripts (`npm ls`/lockfile `hasInstallScript`), and **whether anything is a native module or ships a platform binary** (`.node`, `*.dll`, `*.dylib`, `*.so`, per-platform `optionalDependencies`: the allowed set is Linux x64; list every `.node` in the head's `node_modules` that the standalone folder carries, with its ELF header check, as `deploy-package.py` does). Advisories as CI runs them: `npm audit --omit=dev --audit-level=high`, `node scripts/audit-dev.mjs` (the dated C-44 exception only, as base), `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` (and restore's NuGetAudit, which fails on any advisory), both at head and base, rc and counts (RELAYED prod audit 0). Also `npm ls @opentelemetry/api` (one copy or two? Next loads the app's own first, RELAYED `tracer.js:55`) and whether a second copy of any OTel package is bundled twice. The exporter is **beta**: say so as a risk (Note), not a defect. The Dependabot alert #1 (RELAYED high on main, unexamined): one `gh api repos/datasecau/HPSM-POC/dependabot/alerts?state=open` GET; the PR adds packages, so say whether any new package is in an alert; a 403 or empty answer is UNKNOWN.
7. **Cost claim (A$4.62/month; `STATUS:67-78`): arithmetic and inputs only, no Azure.** Re-add the table (RELAYED total 16.2 MB/day wire), apply the 2x billed factor, x30, to GB, the A$4.7582/GB rate (RELAYED `B410_STATUS.md:76`; read that line), the 5 GB free allowance (shared by the billing account, UNMEASURED), the A$10 stop line (about 2.1 GB), the cap worst case (`dailyQuotaGb: 1` at `infra/modules/monitoring.bicep:22`: about 30 GB, A$142.75). Check each input: the assumed load (1,000 web, 3,000 API requests/day; 5 SQL dependencies per request) is ASSUMED, say what changes if SQL spans are 20 per request or the loopback fixture's wire sizes are measured with a longer exception; **measure the bytes per request and per error row from YOUR OWN capture of check 2** and say whether it agrees within 20% with 700 / 760 / 620 / 2,070. Say whether the drop rules (health, static, the outer routing span) cut rows as the STATUS says and whether the 1.0 sampling ratio plus a bot scan could exceed the cap. A mismatch between the claim's arithmetic and its inputs is a finding; the claim's truth on Azure is NOT TESTED.
8. **Completion vs commission, and no person-visible string.** Table every item: the STATUS `PRIOR WORK` section (each `git log -S` count re-run on `git --no-optional-locks` at the sha's parents with its zero control `-S'zzz-no-such-string-7f3a'`; Jira is NOT re-queried by you), design items **D1-D5**, and Done-when **(1)-(5)** (brief `:14`): for each say **DONE in Phase A, Phase B (needs ADDENDUM-1 and a deploy), or NOT DONE**. Expected: (1) positive-control rows seen on UAT = Phase B; (2) privacy = Phase A tests, Phase B scan; (3) cost = Phase B measurement; (4) PR + CodeQL = not yet (no PR); (5) UAT live check = Phase B. D5 (no fault route added, ruled in Q1): confirm no new route/endpoint/flag whose job is to throw (grep `api/src` and `web/src` additions; the test-only fault host in `api/tests/` is not product). `infra/README.md` (+18): the Telemetry paragraph: what it says is sent/never sent, query hint, cost line; judge each claim against your checks 2-7 (a claim you disproved is a finding), no person's name, no "never/always/every" about Azure behaviour that nobody measured. **No person-visible string added:** over all added lines in `api/src` and `web/src` (non-test), every string literal is a setting name, an attribute key, a route template, a constant log template or a message that names no value, and **0 are rendered to a browser** (`web/src/app/**` and components untouched: prove by program; control: a planted `"Welcome, reviewers"` is flagged); the web's one `console.log` line (RELAYED constant text + an error NAME): quote it. Also CodeQL classes the builder expects (log injection, sensitive data in logs on `ScrubbingProcessors.cs` and the `console.log`): say what you read; **CI/CodeQL at the branch sha** (`gh api repos/datasecau/HPSM-POC/commits/837056ca…/check-runs --paginate`, `code-scanning/analyses?ref=refs/heads/b429/telemetry-224`, open alerts on that ref; with no PR, runs may not exist: "not scanned yet" is never "clean"; quote what you read at start, mid and verdict).

## SEVERITY / VERDICT
Blocker: **any canary or personal-data item found in the scrubbed payload on either app** (including a resource attribute, a metric attribute, a Statsbeat field, an exception stack value, a log scope); a processor that fails open (exports unscrubbed on a throw or an unknown key); telemetry active, a socket opened or an exporter started with no connection string; an exporter that blocks or fails a request or crashes start-up when the receiver is down or the string is bad; `register()` delayed or the warm-ups changed; the exemption wider than exact path equality (any of the four refusal rows or your extras passing), or a `.node` exempt; `deploy-package.py web` not rc 0 on the Linux-equivalent package (after the Mac-only artefact is left out); a lost test name; a failing test or build rc != 0; a weakened or edited existing expectation; a path beyond the 21 (infra modules/env, `.github`, `UatOpenAuthentication.cs`); a non-Linux native module that would ship; `npm audit` / NuGetAudit failing; a secret; a person-visible string added; a fault route added. Major: a surviving mutant (the builder's or yours); an instrument control that does not fire (a dead canary); a measured size that disagrees with the cost table by more than 20% with the A$ line moving across the A$10 stop line; a README claim you disproved; Statsbeat or live metrics sending something not stated; a CI failure that is neither tracked nor caused by this change. Minor: an unclear comment, a new row that passes against base without a red proof and without a "control" label. Note: the exporter is a beta; the API exception row is Phase-A-only and Phase B must say NOT RUN (Q1 ruling 3); Dependabot #1; the `signin-budget` timeout; the A$ claim's truth on Azure; the 5 GB free allowance. Overall **GO** · **GO WITH FINDINGS** · **NO GO**; add ` (CI pending: <names>)` / ` (CI red: <names>)` / ` (no PR yet: CodeQL not run)` as measured at the verdict.
First line of STATUS: `GATE VERDICT B431: <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO> @ 837056c (EQ <21 paths, 5 commits, 0 outside partition, existing tests edited n> · privacy <canaries n planted, n found scrubbed, n in the stock control, dead canaries n, extra items hunted n, found n; both apps y/n> · inert <no string: sockets 0 y/n, register ms, warm-ups unchanged y/n, signin-warmup:92 green y/n; dead receiver ok y/n> · exemption <exact-equality rows n of n, extras n of n, web package rc n at head vs base n> · suites <api n/n, web n/n, infra n/n, names lost n, added 65/44/2, build rc n, gitleaks rc n> · mutants <builder n of 6+ red, own n of 3 red, survivors <names|none>> · deps <new n, native non-Linux n, audit rc n n n, licences ok y/n> · cost <arithmetic ok y/n, measured bytes within 20% y/n> · completion <Phase A done n of 5+5, Phase B n> · visible words 0 · CI/CodeQL <state>)`. Then: Step 0 sha256s and slot count · REFUSE counts · PINS (start, mid, verdict: branch name beside every sha) · instrument (dotnet, node, bicep, python versions, load per heavy start) · checks 1-8 each with FAIL condition (clock), evidence path, result, frame · findings `B431-n` (severity, `path:line` at the sha, instrument, FAIL met, evidence class MEASURED AT RUNTIME / PROBED / READ ONLY, fix-shape in prose) · **FOR TUESDAY** (open the PR only on GO/GWF; Phase B prerequisites; the deploy package CI will see; the cost line to carry; anything for the daily cap card) · FOUND / TESTED / HOW / NOT TESTED / corrections / processes and trees left · **UNMEASURED**. **Last line, exactly:** `VERDICT: B431 b429/telemetry-224 @ 837056c on main <sha7>: telemetry 224 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO> <token>` (main by `ls-remote` at verdict; CI suffix per above) or `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <one question>`.

